   3  4 11 	1	120.0	20.0 ; ether backbone to tail angle validated on DHPCE and DMPCE
   3  5  6 	1	180.0	13.5 ; ether backbone to tail angle validated on DHPCE and DMPCE
   5  6  7 	1      180.0	13.5   ; can be used with CBT dihedral potential, fitted from charmm36 reference
   6  7  8 	1      180.0	13.5   ; across a beads containing a double bond in the first/third bead
   7  8  9 	1      140.0	10.0   ; one unsaturation
   8  9 10 	1      180.0	13.5   ; identical to a_C1_C1_C1 to improve transition temperatures of singly unsaturated lipids
   4 11 12 	1	180.0	13.5 ; ether backbone to tail angle validated on DHPCE and DMPCE
  11 12 13 	1      180.0	13.5   ; can be used with CBT dihedral potential, fitted from charmm36 reference
  12 13 14 	1      180.0	13.5   ; across a beads containing a double bond in the first/third bead
  13 14 15 	1      140.0	10.0   ; one unsaturation
  14 15 16 	1      180.0	13.5   ; identical to a_C1_C1_C1 to improve transition temperatures of singly unsaturated lipids



;;;;;; Martini lipid topology for di-C18:2 EG (DLEG), generated using:
; The Martini lipid itp generator version M3.l01  Args are: -alname DLEG -alhead 'G P' -allink 'E E' -altail 'CDDC CDDC'
; WARNING: Autogenerated and not all lipid headgroup and tail combinations have been tested;
;          used with care and see K.B. Pedersen et al. 2024 for guidance.
;
; Description:
;   A general model ether lipid phosphatidylglycerol (EG) lipid corresponding to atomistic C18:2(9c;12c) dilinoleoyl (DLEG or DLiEG) tails.
; Parameterization:
;   This topology follows the standard Martini 3.0 lipid definitions and building block rules. 
;   Bonded parameters and mapping have been optimized as described in K.B. Pedersen et al. 2024.
; Reference(s): 
; K.B. Pedersen et al., The Martini 3 Lipidome: Expanded and Refined Parameters Improve Lipid Phase Behavior*, 
; ACS Central Science, 2025. doi: 10.1021/acscentsci.5c00755
; P.C.T. Souza et al., Martini 3: A General Purpose Force Field for Coarse-Grained Molecular Dynamics*, 
; Nature Methods, 2021. doi: 10.1038/s41592-021-01098-3
; Created: 2024.07.12
;
; Molecular topology and mapping of indices:
; GL0-PO4-ET1-C1A-D2A-D3A-C4A
;          |
;         ET2-C1B-D2B-D3B-C4B
;
;  1 - 2 - 3 - 5 - 6 - 7 - 8 
;          |
;          4 - 9 - 10- 11- 12
;
;@INSANE alhead=G P, allink=E E, altail=CDDC CDDC, alname=DLEG, charge=-1.0
;@RESNTEST DLE==DLEG if: atoms[0]==GL0
;@BEADS GL0 PO4 ET1 ET2 C1A D2A D3A C4A C1B D2B D3B C4B 
;@BONDS GL0-PO4 PO4-ET1 PO4-ET2 ET1-ET2 ET1-C1A C1A-D2A D2A-D3A D3A-C4A ET2-C1B C1B-D2B D2B-D3B D3B-C4B 
;

